llm_calls.content:
{
  "selected_feature_id": 7,
  "rationale": "Usual weekly hours worked adds strong, broadly state-invariant signal for income beyond education: more hours generally correspond to greater labor earnings, especially distinguishing full-time from part-time work. It is more semantically tied to the target and less likely than occupation, birthplace, race, or sex to encode brittle geographic or demographic shortcuts."
}

